  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The proposal fails to demonstrate that the property is suitable for conversion; the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the original dwellinghouse is greater than 130 square metres in area, and therefore fails the minimum size threshold to be eligible for conversion. The proposal also fails to demonstrate that the property is located a reasonable walking distance from town centre facilities. The proposal is therefore unacceptable in principle, contrary to Local Plan Policy SC10. ",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposal does not provide appropriate numbers of cycle storage facilities and inadequate access to the cycle parking provision, which would lead to an unsatisfactory development of the site and would fail to promote sustainable forms of transport contrary to Local Plan Policy EC2, London Plan Policy T5 and the West London Cycle Parking Guidance.\r\n",
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal would result in the loss of a satisfactory family dwelling unit and not suitable for conversion due to the original dwellinghouse is less than 130 square metres in area; and in a location with low public transport accessibility and location of an unreasonable walking distance from town centre facilities which the Council considers to be suitable for continued residential use in order to help meet the demand for such accommodation as a house. The proposal is therefore unacceptable in principle, contrary to policies H9, H10, T3 of London Plan and Local Plan policies SC10, EC2.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal does not provide appropriate numbers of cycle storage facilities and inadequate access to the cycle parking provision, which would lead to an unsatisfactory development of the site and would fail to promote sustainable forms of transport contrary to Local Plan Policy EC2, London Plan Policy T5 and the West London Cycle Parking Guidance."
